---
// Staged Slack mockup. Synthetic workspace, channel and data only.
---

<div
  class="sk"
  role="img"
  aria-label="Illustrative Slack mockup. In the acme-launch channel you ask marko for the launch-week plan in a thread. marko replies with three bullets: Tuesday blog post, Wednesday email to 1,240 people, Thursday social thread, and says drafts are in the shared doc."
>
  <div class="sk-side" aria-hidden="true">
    <b class="sk-ws">Acme</b>
    <span class="sk-ch"># general</span>
    <span class="sk-ch on"># acme-launch</span>
    <span class="sk-ch"># ops</span>
    <span class="sk-sec">Apps</span>
    <span class="sk-ch"><i class="sk-dot"></i>marko</span>
    <span class="sk-ch"><i class="sk-dot"></i>klanker</span>
  </div>
  <div class="sk-main" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="sk-head"># acme-launch</div>
    <div class="sk-msg">
      <span class="sk-ava you">Y</span>
      <div>
        <p class="sk-who">you <span>10:12</span></p>
        <p>@marko what's the plan for launch week?</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sk-msg">
      <span class="sk-ava tg-ava a2">m</span>
      <div>
        <p class="sk-who">marko <em>APP</em> <span>10:12</span></p>
        <p>Three beats, all drafted:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Tue</b> · blog post, case study up top</li>
          <li><b>Wed</b> · launch email to 1,240</li>
          <li><b>Thu</b> · social thread, 6 posts</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Drafts are in the launch doc. Say go on any of them.</p>
        <p class="sk-thread">3 replies · last reply just now</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
